      ['Ribosome and subunit','A ribosome builds proteins. Its two subunits are parts made of RNA and proteins that join to form the working structure.'],
      ['Translation','Using an mRNA message to join amino-acid building blocks into a protein chain.'],
      ['Nucleolus','A region inside the nucleus with no surrounding membrane. It makes much of the rRNA and assembles early ribosomal subunits.'],
      ['Nuclear export','Movement out of the nucleus into the cell interior outside it, not release outside the whole cell.'],
      ['Secretion and exocytosis','Secretion releases material outside a cell. In exocytosis, a small membrane-enclosed carrier joins the outer cell membrane and releases its contents outside.'],
      ['Localization signal','Information in a molecule that can help cellular machinery direct it to a particular compartment.']
